  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Life-Saving Assistance to Protection and Resilience Building of Disaster Affected Communities and Vulnerable People on the Move</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The crisis in Somalia is one of the most long-standing and complex in the world due to ongoing armed conflict, insecurity, and recurrent climatic shocks. In addition to that, in 2021 Somalia faced political tensions due to delayed elections. Despite progress over the last years, an increasing number of people are in need of humanitarian support. The project intends to support vulnerable Somalia communities, affected by conflict and natural disasters, through firstly disaster preparedness, response, and resilience building. Secondly, community members vulnerable to or affected by human trafficking are being reached through awareness raising campaigns on trafficking or receiving direct assistance. Both interventions contribute to the realization of human security and foster peace, stability and improved economic conditions, targeting disaster affected populations and vulnerable people on the move in hard-to-reach area.</narrative>
  </description>
